      "writtenOn": "2021-06-21T23:17:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Basically LGTM, modulo a few nits.\n\u003e \n\u003e It looks like this does not add zygote memory allocation, except in the case of an app zygote?\n\nUnfortunately, I think it does allocate from the heap in general case, when we do fds_to_ignore.insert(). Christian also wanted to avoid extra allocations. Count me as +1: it would be a nice refactor to reuse the same fds_to_close and fds_to_ignore as read-only after the first fork - will save a few pages once in a while.\n\nI\u0027d prefer to do it in a separate change (likely several changes) - much less trivial than this one, and will require more testing. Also this may be relevant to\nyour other plans for the zygote(s) - I\u0027d be interested to learn about them, though without clear commitments at this point.\n\nWe have similar allocations a few lines above, those will hopefully go away after the refactor. At least for now this pattern is compact in one place, leaving some hope of it getting removed some day :)",
      "parentUuid": "94b8a038_ad77afd6",
      "revId": "ed10978de1dda9abc85c1736e2ffbc3d995cb03c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
