      "lineNbr": 2562,
      "author": {
        "id": 1054754
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-06-22T11:39:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e My impression is that conditional call to fail_fn would be consistent with the style here?\n\nFor the purpose of asserting on an internal invariant the fail_fn looks a little too verbose, with some effects not locally controlled. Choosing to omit the explicit check and SEGV in case the invariant is broken. Something like CHECK macro would be useful to have, even without a message, to show that the maintainer(s) did not forget their nullability invariants.",
      "parentUuid": "bdf222d6_d4baec3e",
